# 09. Agent economics

Prepared locally behind `POSTLAUNCH_FEATURES=agent-economics`. `/agents/:id/` displays canonical Selection registry events and spendable Vault balance at the indexed block. Daily gross income, fees, net income, burn and owner subsidies remain separate exact base-unit amounts. Registry-classified income is labeled as such; independent earned-income provenance remains unknown, and unclassified transfers are excluded.

Date filters, coverage boundaries, limited lifecycle rows and stale data are explicit. Unindexed days show no coverage rather than zero. Canonical block and dataset checks bracket the balance read; reorgs and unavailable sources withhold economics. No configured Selection means not configured, not generated agent activity. Current CPU-only production requires a separately configured Selection deployment before populated data is available.

Validation: 9 persisted-index tests cover actual event projection, monetary precision, subsidies, coverage, lineage, reorg and balance failures. This change performs no on-chain action.
